{"_id":"68d3df02166b018f83df5d55","roadmapSlug":"html","nodeId":"nOIijMH-3TvcO1KL6qzwf","description":"# Tags and Attributes\n\nTags and attributes are fundamental building blocks of HTML. Tags define the structure and content of a webpage, such as headings, paragraphs, and images. Attributes provide additional information about HTML elements, modifying their behavior or appearance, like specifying the source of an image or the destination of a link.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Tags | MDN docs","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Tag","_id":"6a71e295b0650226a59f1bc2"},{"type":"article","title":"Attributes | MDN docs","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Attribute","_id":"6a71e295b0650226a59f1bc3"},{"type":"video","title":"HTML - Tags | W3Schools","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vIoO52MdZFE","_id":"6a71e295b0650226a59f1bc4"},{"type":"video","title":"HTML - Attributes | W3Schools","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yMX901oVtn8","_id":"6a71e295b0650226a59f1bc5"}],"createdAt":"2025-09-24T12:07:30.984Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-04T13:01:09.024Z","lessonPacks":[{"_id":"6a10b41ba95e0d5c68dede2f","title":"HTML Fundamentals","slug":"html","description":"Enough HTML to read, write, inspect, and understand real web pages.","lessonIds":["6a0da437a95e0d5c68ded033","6a0ef00da95e0d5c68ded162","6a0f1366a95e0d5c68ded2b4","6a0f2262a95e0d5c68ded32a","6a0f33e7a95e0d5c68ded463","6a102d2fa95e0d5c68ded758","6a106a2ba95e0d5c68deda00","6a107b29a95e0d5c68deda53"],"projectIds":["68b7185fffbff9183d772aea","68b7185fffbff9183d772aeb","6a1485bfac1c5fa9928a2087","6a1485c5ac1c5fa9928a2093","6a1485cbac1c5fa9928a2099","6a1485d1ac1c5fa9928a20a4"],"featuredImage":"","readingTime":58,"lessonCount":8,"quizCount":0,"projectCount":6}],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/html/content/nOIijMH-3TvcO1KL6qzwf.md"}